{
  "summary": "The Lean statement bounds a derivative-word of the parametric torus inverse `inverse d f` at a slow parameter p by an explicit constant `mixedLossConstant (w.length) * C`. It assumes smoothness, periodicity, and C bounds on f's slice and on x-jets of order `w.length+5` over the unit square. This is a parametric, quantitative analogue of (8.19), not the paper's statement. The key caveat is that `Source`, `Plane`, `inverse`, `slice`, `coordinatePartial`, `omega`, `weight`, `Frequency`, `Direction`, `Periodic` and `swapFunction` are not shown, so fidelity cannot be fully verified. The statement also differs structurally from (8.19), which has a generic constant C_m and a C^{m+4} norm.", 
  "glossary": [
    {"decl": "partialX", "line": 4, "plain": "∂/∂x of f at z, computed as the Fréchet derivative in direction (1,0).", "standard_concept": "first coordinate partial derivative", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": ""},
    {"decl": "xJet", "line": 6, "plain": "p-fold iterate of ∂x applied to f.", "standard_concept": "∂_x^p f", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": ""},
    {"decl": "derivativeWord", "line": 9, "plain": "Applies a list of coordinate partials (x or y per Bool) successively to f.", "standard_concept": "mixed partial derivative of order |w|", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "`coordinatePartial` is not shown; which Bool means x or y is not specified."},
    {"decl": "mixedLossConstant", "line": 14, "plain": "(6‖ω⁻¹‖‖ω‖^r)·3^(r+5)·∑_{k} (weight k ^4)⁻¹.", "standard_concept": "explicit constant C_m in (8.19)", "matches_standard": "partly", "note": "Paper gives an unspecified C_m. The tsum is junk 0 if not summable, which would make the bound vacuous; summability is not in the excerpt. `weight`, `omega` and `Frequency` are undefined here."},
    {"decl": "norm_derivativeWord_inverse_le", "line": 19, "plain": "For smooth periodic parametric source f and a word w, ‖D^w (inverse d f)(p, Y)‖ ≤ mixedLossConstant(|w|)·C, where C bounds f and its x-jets of order |w|+5 (and the swapped function's) on [0,1]² for the slice at p.", "standard_concept": "Lemma 8.6 bound (8.19) with parameters", "matches_standard": "partly", "note": "Pointwise bound at Y with hypotheses only on the unit square, relying on periodicity. Hypotheses use x-derivatives, not full C^{m+4} norms."}
  ],
  "lean_claims": [
    {"theorem": "norm_derivativeWord_inverse_le", "line": 19, "plain": "Given direction d, smooth (C^∞) periodic source f on P × Plane, word w, parameter p, point Y, and constant C such that on [0,1]² ‖f(p,·)‖ ≤ C, ‖∂x^{|w|+5} f(p,·)‖ ≤ C, and ‖∂x^{|w|+5} of the swapped slice‖ ≤ C, then ‖D^w (slice (inverse d f) p)(Y)‖ ≤ mixedLossConstant(|w|)·C."}
  ],
  "paper_claims": [
    {"ref": "Lemma 8.6 / (8.19)", "plain": "For smooth zero-mean F on T², N φ = F has a unique smooth zero-mean solution N⁻¹F given by the Fourier series Σ F̂(k)/(2πi vt·k) e^{2πik·y}, with ‖N⁻¹F‖_{C^m_y} ≤ C_m ‖F‖_{C^{m+4}_y} for every m ≥ 0."}
  ],
  "coverage": [
    {"paper_ref": "(8.19) norm bound", "lean_theorem": "norm_derivativeWord_inverse_le", "relation": "different", "why": "Parametric version with an explicit constant, controlled by sup bounds of x-jets (order |w|+5) rather than a C^{m+4} norm in y; the unit-square pointwise form and the hypotheses on the swapped function are not matched in the excerpt."},
    {"paper_ref": "Lemma 8.6 existence/uniqueness/Fourier formula/zero mean", "lean_theorem": null, "relation": "not_formalized", "why": "The theorem under audit covers only the norm bound, not existence, uniqueness, the series formula, or zero mean."}
